# Repository Boundaries

Before editing, decide which boundary owns the request:

- Workload lifecycle, `/manage/*`, provider adapters, remote resource control:
  `aqp_control_plane/`.
- Shared value types, ABCs, auth/resource filters, topology, stable wire
  contracts: `aqp_platform_core/`.
- Operator UI, client API wrappers, WebSocket client behavior (local
  power users): `aqp_client/` under the `aqp_client/` boundary.
- Cloud-hosted customer-facing PaaS frontend (public marketing site +
  auth-gated dashboard, dual Auth0/Entra identity, multi-tenant):
  `aqp_ui/`. HTTP-only against `aqp_control_plane` and the AQP API.
- Internal admin surface (AQP staff at `manage.aqp.fund`, audit-first):
  `aqp_admin/`. HTTP-only against `aqp_control_plane` and the AQP API.
- Curated external-code knowledge, prompts, rules, skills:
  `aqp_snippets/`, `extractions/`, or `.cursor/`.
- Bot templates and samples: `aqp_bots/` and `aqp_bots/templates/`.
- Bot runtime behavior stays in `aqp_bots/` until extraction interfaces
  exist.
- Quant runtime domains (agents, RL, analysis, backtests, data, persistence,
  tasks) stay in `aqp/`.

Read `aqp_docs/docs/concepts/platform/repository-split.md` and the nearest `AGENTS.md` before moving
source across boundaries.

